From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:49:02 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 43/60] Meridian: Safe Browsing lists over v4

Non-Google builds take Chromium's field-trial testing config, which turns on
SafeBrowsingLocalListsUseSBv5; the v5 list endpoint answers 404 to any key but
Chrome's, so no lists were ever downloaded. Without that study the lists come
over v4 with Meridian's key, and phishing and malware warnings work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
